at sets it apart is  that does have optical image  stabilization and this is the first in  any samsung galaxy phone apart from the  zoom series so overall it takes really  good photos and videos but some people  may notice that it's a bit over  sharpened now it's not the end of the  world but you may find that some photos  don't look 100% natural videography is  also quite fun with the optical image  stabilization making it easier to get  some nice steady looking shots and of  course slow motion video makes return  with the ability to shoot at 240 frames  per second at 720p so as you can see  here this was just something randomly  happening at my shopping centre down the  road and yeah as you can see it turns  out pretty interesting and you can just  seal all the details that happen so  quickly in real life and it's just kind  of fun so overall I give the camera  about an 8.5 out of 10 few points  deducted for the over sharpening and  fairly poor low-light performance it is  improved over last year's Galaxy Note 3  but it's still not the best in the world  and here's an example of that this is  just some random low-light shots that I  took and as you can see some of the  footage is just a little bit grainy okay  so that covers most things we're almost  done with the review but before we  finish off and know you wrap this up  let's just go over a couple of quick  things  firstly the battery life so in here  you're getting a three thousand two  hundred and twenty milliamp hour battery  and it can quickly charge from zero to  fifty percent in about thirty minutes  which is very very handy and I and I  really like the better in this device  looking at about five to six hours of  screen on time and you should be able to  get through a full day with would  moderate to heavy use and once again it  does depend on which version of the  phone you pick up some people have said  that they've had a not as good battery  life but for me personally and this  phone that I've had battery life has  been quite good I wouldn't say you would  have to worry about carrying a second  battery or something like that and  finally something that's a bit different  that no other phone manufacturer has  done actually and that is virtual  reality and this is going to be coming  to the note series quite soon so for  those of you that don't know virtual  reality is a technology that has existed  for the better part of three decades now  but it has never really been realized  until earlier last year when a company  called oculus released a virtual reality  headset and it was spearheaded by a man  called John Carmack and this was the guy  that basically invented side scrolling  for PC before was only a console thing  back in the early 90s and also created  basically 3d gaming with his home built  game engine for games such as  Wolfenstein 3d and doom so he is a big  big player in the game industry and so  he worked on this virtual reality  headset yes up just since then the  virtuality community has started to take  off and now Samsung has teamed up with  oculus and John Carmack and together  they've released this virtual reality  headset system for the Galaxy Note 4 so  virtual reality is a thing that is hard  to demonstrate but really it is what it  sounds like it is an entire world where  you put on these goggles and there's an  entire world that you can explore and  feel like you're totally immersed within  this other realm so it's an interesting  technology and um  Samsung is spearheading this at the very  forefront of a mobile version of this  with the note 4 so the way it works is  the note 4 will act as the virtual  reality screen and then there will be a  system called the gear VR which will act  as the goals and basically the rest of  the virtual reality systems all you have  to do is slot your phone into the  of the gear VR and then you have a  virtual reality system where you can  play games or just watch movies inside a  virtual cinema so basically you can turn  around and see the seats behind you or  that kind of thing so yeah a whole bunch  of stuff happening with virtual reality  and it's going to be interesting to see  what Samsung does in the future with  that and as a side point me and a friend  are working on a virtual reality app for  the gear system so we'll see how that  goes so on that note I think it is time  to conclude this review so what have we  learnt so far the Galaxy Note 4 is a  great all-round phone that does a bit of  everything and does it all fairly well  so with an industry that's getting more  and more crowded in phone tablets making  the transformation of being laughed at  to being the global trend the note 4 is  in a good position right now and sum it  up succinctly in one sentence the note 4  is the note series realized and done  right  all the little improvements over last  year's model really created a pleasing  synergy that was a major improvement  over every note or any previous Samsung  device for that matter so what is the  overall score well this phone receives  an 85 percent which is a very solid  score and with all the additional  features some of which I didn't even go  through the valley is much greater than  most of the competition out there so if  you're looking for a premium device and  you just want to go out there and get  the very best I say this phone is  definitely one you should look at anyway  this has been cold fusion thank you for  sitting down and choosing to click on  this video right here on YouTube and as  usual don't forget to rate comment and  subscribe and if you like this video and  think that someone would benefit from  what I've said feel free to send a link  across so you can share it and yeah  until next time I'll catch you again  soon for the next video and enjoy the  rest of your day guys everyone Cheers  cold future  it's rethinking
 

